### 4. 🟡 Missing Security Headers
**Severity: Medium**

Express by default sends an `X-Powered-By: Express` header (fingerprinting) and sets **none** of the standard security headers (`Content-Security-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, etc.).

**Fix:** Add `helmet`:
```js
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());            // sets 11 security headers automatically
app.disable('x-powered-by'); // belt-and-suspenders removal of fingerprint
```

---

### 5. 🟡 No Rate Limiting (Broken Authentication / DoS)
**Severity: Medium**

There is no rate limiting on any route. This enables brute-force attacks on future auth endpoints and trivial denial-of-service.

**Fix:** Add `express-rate-limit`:
